It returns `LocalZone.instance` — the `LocalZone` singleton (`type === "local"`, valid), not `null`/`undefined`, and it does not throw.

```js
static get defaultZone() {
  return defaultZone || LocalZone.instance;
}
```

The module-level `defaultZone` starts as `null` (with the comment "not setting this directly to LocalZone.instance bc loading order issues"), and `normalizeZone` is only used by the `defaultZoneName` setter, not the getter.

