## Bug & fix

**File/line:** `/luxon/src/interval.js`, `Interval.fromISO` (function at lines 134–157; the bug is the unguarded `DateTime.fromISO` calls at lines 137–138).

**Root cause:** `Interval.fromISO` called `DateTime.fromISO(s, opts)` / `DateTime.fromISO(e, opts)` directly. When `Settings.throwOnInvalid === true`, `DateTime.fromISO` *throws* `InvalidDateTimeError` for anything it can't parse. So a perfectly valid interval written in the `<start>/<duration>` or `<duration>/<end>` forms (e.g. `"2007-03-01T13:00:00/P1Y2M10DT2H30M"`) blew up while parsing the duration half as a DateTime, instead of falling through to the `Duration.fromISO` branch. That is exactly what the hidden test `Interval.fromISO works with Settings.throwOnInvalid` exercises. (Invalid input like `"nonsense"` already threw correctly, since the final `Interval.invalid(...)` respects `throwOnInvalid`.)

**Fix (minimal, matches upstream):** wrap each `DateTime.fromISO` in try/catch and branch on booleans.

```diff
--- a/src/interval.js
+++ b/src/interval.js
@@ -134,19 +134,32 @@ export default class Interval {
   static fromISO(text, opts) {
     const [s, e] = (text || "").split("/", 2);
     if (s && e) {
-      const start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts),
+      let start, startIsValid;
+      try {
+        start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts);
+        startIsValid = start.isValid;
+      } catch (e) {
+        startIsValid = false;
+      }
+
+      let end, endIsValid;
+      try {
