The default is `'latn'` — i.e. `/\d/` (ASCII digits 0–9).

```js
export function digitRegex({ numberingSystem }, append = "") {
  return new RegExp(`${numberingSystems[numberingSystem || "latn"]}${append}`);
}
```

There is no default parameter value; the fallback comes from `numberingSystem || "latn"`, so `undefined`, `null`, or `""` all yield `latn` (`numberingSystems.latn === "\\d"`). Note an unrecognized non-empty key yields `/undefined/` since there's no validation.

